# Known-benign "possibly lost" reports from program-lifetime lazy_static caches
# in the x509-parser dependency chain. hashbrown stores an interior pointer into
# its allocation, so valgrind cannot see the root held by the static and
# classifies the block as "possibly lost" instead of "still reachable".
{
   x509-parser-extension-parsers-lazy-static
   Memcheck:Leak
   ...
   fun:*EXTENSION_PARSERS*
}
{
   oid-registry-lazy-static
   Memcheck:Leak
   ...
   fun:*OID_REGISTRY*
}
